# Markdown here is hand wrapped and the wrapping carries meaning: TASKS.md rows, the generated
# tables in README.md and FEASIBILITY.md, and the no-dash rule. Prettier would rewrap all of it and
# fight the board lint. Code is formatted, prose is not.
*.md

# Generated by pnpm.
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Written by the record and replay wrapper, not by hand. Formatting recorded provider
# responses is churn that fights the recorder on every re-record, and it would rewrite
# evidence to satisfy a style rule.
fixtures/recorded/

# Same argument, for what a spike writes. result.json comes out of JSON.stringify, which always
# expands arrays, and prettier always collapses the short ones, so every spike run would leave the
# tree unformatted and every re-run would undo the fix. A spike's own recorded responses are
# evidence for the same reason the ones above are. The hand written parts of a spike,
# thresholds.json, mints.json and run.mjs, are formatted normally.
spikes/*/result.json
spikes/*/recorded/
# Recorded chain state, written by a recorder as raw bytes. Prettier does preserve number literals
# verbatim, checked, so this is churn rather than damage: every re-pin writes the file unformatted
# again and leaves the tree dirty. The numbers are the reason it is written as raw bytes in the
# first place, since rentEpoch is u64::MAX and does not survive a JSON round trip.
spikes/*/snapshot.json

# Hand written, and owned by other tasks. The comments in these carry the reasoning for each gate
# and prettier would rewrap them.
.github/

# Agent worktrees are whole checkouts of this repo. Formatting them formats the same files twice
# and fails the check on whatever another branch is mid-edit.
.claude/worktrees/
